--- a/changelog/6947.bugfix.rst
+++ b/changelog/6947.bugfix.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Fixed a regression where functions registered with :meth:`unittest.TestCase.addCleanup` were not being called on test failures: pytest no longer breaks out of the unittest ``TestCase.run`` machinery, so ``tearDown`` and cleanups now run for failing tests. ``tearDown`` is only postponed when ``--pdb`` is active, so the debugger still sees the test instance intact.
